I also have a concern I could not settle by reading the code. The new test uses `a: 'Unknown'`, an unresolvable forward reference. That normally raises `PydanticUndefinedAnnotation`, which subclasses `NameError`, and `GENERATE_SCHEMA_ERRORS` does not include it. If the handler raises it during `InstanceOf.__get_pydantic_core_schema__`, the `except` clause will not catch it. The model would then be left unbuilt instead of falling back to `is_instance_schema`, and the new test would fail. Whether that happens depends on how dataclass field annotations are resolved here.

A human should run the new test in a working environment with a matching pydantic-core."}]}
